cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Beyond Reward Shaping: CVaR-Constrained Reinforcement Learning for Avellaneda–Stoikov Market Making"
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "AA-ron2"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/AA-ron2/cvar-market-making"
abstract: >-
  Code, tests and result tables of an MSc thesis on risk-aware market making. A PPO agent chooses the
  Avellaneda–Stoikov risk aversion and a quote skew on replayed Binance Spot DOGEUSDT order books (25-level
  snapshots, January 2025) with a best-price-reach execution proxy. The thesis compares a penalty-based reward
  design (B2, a drawdown penalty) with a PPO-Lagrangian agent under a CVaR0.2 constraint on the full-day maximum
  drawdown (B3), against unconstrained PPO (B1), a fine-tuned control without a risk term (B1+) and the analytical
  Avellaneda–Stoikov baseline (B0). B3 did not reach its threshold on its training days within k = 10 updates. On 23
  retrospective out-of-sample days, the trading day being the unit of inference, the primary tests give no evidence
  that B3 changes the CVaR0.2 of the daily maximum drawdown relative to B1 or B2; B0 had the lowest CVaR0.2 and the
  highest Sharpe ratio. The repository also holds the pre-registered Hummingbot paper-trading forward test of B0 and
  B3, which is descriptive only.
keywords:
  - market making
  - reinforcement learning
  - constrained Markov decision process
  - CVaR
  - PPO-Lagrangian
  - Avellaneda-Stoikov
  - maximum drawdown
